WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.050
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:10.170
Today I am going to explain an American coming-of-age
comedy-drama film called “Jack.”

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.870
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:18.380
Watch out and take care!

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.820
The movie begins at a Halloween party where
a young woman Karen Powell is dancing with

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.660
her husband Brian Powell.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.970
Suddenly, Karen feels a sharp pain in her
stomach and steps aside from the dance floor.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.890
Brian quickly gets to her and asks her what
is wrong.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.930
It turns out that Karen has been pregnant
for a little more than two months but is going

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.070
into labor.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.480
Brian and their friends rush her to the hospital.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.940
The nurses do not believe her when she says
she is not due for another seven months.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.290
The doctor comes in and calmly tells her that
it might only be some early pregnancy cramps

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.030
but is surprised to see her fully dilated.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.030
With a deep breath, Karen pushes out a fully
developed baby boy.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.570
She holds him in her arms and calls him Jack.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:03.489
The doctors check Jack’s condition and find
out that he has an exaggerated form of Werner

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:04.489
syndrome.

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:08.369
Because of this, his cells are growing four
times faster than the normal rate.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:12.420
Although he should be a two months old infant
right now, he is a fully developed nine months

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.549
old baby.

00:01:16.549 --> 00:01:20.859
The doctor assures the parents that the kid
is perfectly healthy and in good shape.

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:25.899
He explains that nature has given all humans
an internal clock that meters our lifespan

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:27.359
and controls our growth.

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:30.459
Jack’s clock happens to tick faster than
others.

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:34.500
The condition is unheard of so it doesn’t
have any cure but they predict that if the

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.889
kid grows at this rate, he will turn into
a fully grown forty-year-old man at the age

00:01:38.889 --> 00:01:39.889
of ten.

00:01:39.889 --> 00:01:42.149
The parents are in utter disbelief.

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:47.149
Cut to ten years later, as the doctors had
predicted, Jack grows up faster than any human

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:50.289
and appears to be a full-grown man at the
age of ten.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:53.979
Although his appearance affirms otherwise,
Jack is a child by nature.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.649
His parents have never allowed him to step
out of their gated house scared that he will

00:01:57.649 --> 00:02:03.030
get bullied.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.670
The neighbor kids who have only got glimpses
of him through the window, consider him a

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.629
giant monster who eats children.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.690
Lawrence Woodruff is Jack’s teacher who
homeschools him every day.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.370
He is the only person who is close to Jack
other than his parents.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.569
One day, Woodruff is trying to teach Jack
but he keeps on getting distracted by the

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:25.530
kids in the front of his house trying to get
a glimpse of the giant ten-year-old.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.500
To mess with them, Jack throws a gooey eyeball
toy through the window.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.489
Woodruff finally gets him back to study but
notices the sadness in Jack’s eyes.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:38.700
After the class, Woodruff suggests to Karen
and Brian that they send Jack to school.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.409
Karen, being the protective mother she is,
is against the idea.

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:46.579
Woodruff states that they can warn the principal
and prepare the kids for Jack’s arrival

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:51.040
to make it easier for him to fit in but the
parents are still against the idea.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.610
In the evening, Jack and Karen play Marco
polo around the house.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.770
When the game ends, Jack asks Karen if he
is really a giant monster.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.439
He had heard the children talk about him during
the day.

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:05.890
Karen assures him that he is as normal as
any kid his age, which couldn’t be further

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.890
away from the truth.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.150
Before going to sleep, Brian and Karen discuss
if they should really send their kid to school.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:15.560
They are disturbed by Jack coming to their
room wanting to sleep with them because he

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.560
had a nightmare.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.049
The following day, Jack is told that he is
going to school for the very first time.

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:24.159
He excitedly shaves his beard and puts on
his clothes.

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:27.099
Karen packs him food and they make their way
to the school.

00:03:27.099 --> 00:03:29.829
They meet the principal McGhee who welcomes
Jack.

00:03:29.829 --> 00:03:31.500
The parents wish him good luck.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.609
Before leaving, Karen asks him to call her
anytime if he gets bullied.

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:38.890
The principal then introduces Jack to his
teacher Miss Marquez.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:42.340
Jack shyly enters the class and stands in
front of his classmates.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.859
The group of kids who were chased away by
him yesterday is also in the same class.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:50.390
Miss Marquez introduces him to the kids and
asks him to take a seat.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.730
Jack then sits on his seat which is too small
for him.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.030
While trying to fit in, he falls off, making
the entire class laugh.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:03.129
Even when he is provided a bigger seat, he
breaks it and the kids laugh even harder.

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:05.999
During recess, he is alone in the playground.

00:04:05.999 --> 00:04:10.480
The children look at him and whisper to each
other about his controversial size.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.780
The group of kids who he chased away the previous
day watches him in fear, believing that he

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.290
will probably beat them for bothering him.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:22.270
The group leader, Louis, brings out the monster
eye from his bag and shows it to Jack but

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:24.270
quickly keeps it back inside.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.990
Just then, a rival group challenges them for
a basketball match.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:32.380
As Jack watches them play, two little girls
poke him with a stick and ask him how old

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.380
he is.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.620
They make fun of his receding hairline and
his hairy arms.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.460
After he sends them away, the basketball lands
near him.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.750
He picks it up to throw it back but the rival
kids say they do not want to touch the ball

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.160
since it is probably contaminated now that
Jack touched it.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.530
Louis and his group clearly feel bad for him.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:54.169
Jack sulks when he returns home and doesn’t
eat his favorite food that Karen cooked.

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:58.310
Brian tells him about the day he first rode
a bicycle and points out how much he has improved

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.310
since.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:03.020
Using the example, he makes Jack understand
that the children at school will eventually

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.250
open up to him.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.800
The following day during lunch, Jack gets
into a tunnel to eat since he has no one to

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:09.900
eat with.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.789
Miss Marquez feels bad for the kid and eats
with him.

00:05:12.789 --> 00:05:16.229
Louis and his friends are challenged to a
basketball match yet again.

00:05:16.229 --> 00:05:19.290
Since they are short on teammates, Louis invites
Jack to play with them.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.720
For the first few rounds, Jack doesn’t understand
what he should do.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.949
But as he gets a hang of it, he scores the
most and makes Louis’s team win for the

00:05:26.949 --> 00:05:28.490
first time.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:32.310
Following that, they are in Miss Marquez’s
class where she asks them to write an essay

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.560
about what they want to be in the future.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:40.440
She pays extra attention to Jack because of
his specialties.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.440
Jack, on the other hand, starts to develop
a crush on his teacher.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.069
After school, Jack thanks Louis for letting
him play.

00:05:47.069 --> 00:05:50.169
Louis, in turn, asks him for another favor.

00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:54.110
He wants him to pretend to be the principal
in front of his mother Dolores so he wouldn’t

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:58.539
get in trouble for not doing his homework.

00:05:58.539 --> 00:06:02.690
Jack is skeptical about the idea but Louis
doesn’t give him time to explain.

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:06.720
Dolores arrives at the school and introduces
herself to Jack, believing that he is the

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.720
principal.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.509
She tells him that she has recently gotten
divorced and Louis is acting out because of

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:12.509
it.

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:14.990
As she talks, Jack only gives her one-word
answers.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:18.960
He ends the conversation after claiming that
Louis is the smartest kid in the school and

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.590
she shouldn’t worry about him.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:25.010
Before leaving, Dolores gives him her number
asking him out for lunch sometime.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.830
Louis thanks Jack for having his back and
takes him in his group.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.569
That day Jack returns home happier than ever.

00:06:31.569 --> 00:06:35.550
He runs around the house and calls his father
at work telling him everything that happened

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.810
throughout the day.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:40.699
On the weekend, Louis knocks on his door and
invites him for a sleepover.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:44.230
Karen is surprised to see how quickly Jack
was able to make friends.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:48.210
She allows the two to go over to Louis’s
home but they cycle back to a treehouse that

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.090
Louis and the group hang out in.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:54.729
The other kids do not want to let Jack in
the group but Louis shows them the adult magazine

00:06:54.729 --> 00:06:57.319
that Jack was able to get for him on the way.

00:06:57.319 --> 00:07:00.730
Seeing that they can probably get a lot of
favors from him, they accept him into the

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.730
group.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.900
They talk about girls and alcohol and have
farting competitions all night.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:10.140
Meanwhile, Karen misses her kid since he has
been away from home for the first time in

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.150
ten years.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:15.750
Brian finds her inside the box that Jack often
plays with and tells her that their kid growing

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.180
up is a good thing.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.240
The following day at school, the kids take
a class picture for the yearbook.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.840
Starting that day, Jack becomes an inseparable
member of the group.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.960
They hang out at the treehouse almost every
day, go trick or treating on Halloween, and

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:34.820
Jack buys more adult magazines for his friends.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:39.030
One day, he even brings Woodruff into the
treehouse and lets him in the group after

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.410
making him eat a gross smoothie bowl.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.419
However, the treehouse cannot handle all that
weight and breaks.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:48.099
As time passes, Jack grows older.

00:07:48.099 --> 00:07:53.000
He starts to lose hair and go bald because
of which he uses black gel on his hair.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.910
His classmates start to submit their essays
about what they want to be in the future but

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.759
Jack hasn’t decided yet.

00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:03.270
A girl says she wants to get married by twenty-eight
but when Jack does the math, he finds out

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.590
he can only marry when he is one hundred and
twelve years old.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.190
He mutters to himself that he wants to be
alive when he grows up.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:14.190
After class, he asks Miss Marquez to be his
date for the dance.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:19.990
As she tries to explain they cannot go together,
he kisses her.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:21.750
Miss Marquez is taken back.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:26.050
She bluntly tells Jack that he is just a child
so they cannot go together.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:29.870
She apologizes to him but he breaks down crying
and runs away.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:34.050
However, his day gets worse when he trips
and falls on the stairs.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:38.100
He is immediately rushed to the hospital where
his parents come running, worried for their

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.100
son.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.720
The doctor claims that Jack’s body has suffered
a severe strain because of the rate of his

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:43.930
cell multiplication.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:49.030
Hence, his internal clock is starting to run
out, meaning he doesn’t have that many years

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:50.130
to live.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:54.650
After returning home, Karen tells Jack that
they have decided to withdraw him from school

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.190
for his own safety.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:00.040
Jack throws a tantrum because he doesn’t
want to be separated from his friends.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:04.270
He begs Brain to let him go back to school
but the parents know they cannot allow that

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.440
after what happened.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.670
At night, Karen and Brian are talking about
Jack in their room when Jack gets hold of

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.790
the matchbox that has Dolores' number and
the name of a club on it.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:16.780
He sneaks out for the first time and visits
the club.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.830
There, he meets a man named Paul and drinks
with him.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:23.160
A while later, he meets Dolores and they start
to dance.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.390
In the middle of it, she tries to make out
with him.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.700
Jack remembers she is still his friend’s
mother and retreats.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.760
He tries to get away from her but bumps into
a guy in the process.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.790
The man is clearly drunk and starts a fight
with him.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.110
Jack insults him, making the guy punch him
in the face.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:41.670
At the end of the night, Jack ends up in jail
for trashing the club.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.180
Dolores bails him out and drives him back
home.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:48.090
Good thing for Jack, his parents are asleep
so he doesn’t get in trouble.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.210
Two weeks have passed since the incident.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.190
Jack has been sulking in his room all this
time.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.910
His friends come to meet him every day but
he doesn’t come out of the house.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:00.720
Karen calls Woodruff to their house in hopes
that he will persuade Jack to come out of

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:01.720
his room.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.930
Jack talks to him and says that he doesn’t
want to learn stuff that he will probably

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.710
never get to use in his life because he won’t
live long.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:12.950
Some days later, Louis gathers the entire
class in front of Jack’s house to call him

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.260
out to play.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:18.460
The next day, Jack gets out of his room and
decides to go back to school.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.970
His parents allow him to do so, seeing how
happy school makes him.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.150
Everyone in his class is overjoyed to see
him back.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:28.570
Seven years later, Jack and his friends are
at their high school graduation.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.720
He is now much older with grey hair and wrinkles.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:36.730
At the end of the movie, he delivers a speech,
in which he reminds people that life is short,

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.850
and urges them to make their life spectacular.

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:44.150
